  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovation node Botswana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Botswana Red Cross Society (volunteers and staff) and communities living within Botswana</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Botswana</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Botswana Red Cross Society (BRCS) and the Netherlands Red Cross (NLRC) have together been engaged in discussions of forming a collaboration around water management innovation as part of a broader approach to disaster preparedness and building community resilience. The programme has been developed and focuses on water as a primary factor in Botswana&#x2019;s disaster risk outlook.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The partnership&#x2019;s framework revolves around water and has three focus areas that are interconnected and operate against a cross -cutting background of future -oriented climate change adaptation, youth innovation and value creation: (1) Promoting innovative and realistic water access, saving and use environment (smart water); (2) Strength and facilitate harmonious landscapes, and; (3) Building resilient communities. 

The partnership&apos;s overall goal is: &#x201c;An agile and adaptive generation that thinks of the bigger picture: taking care of each other, their community, the environment, the country and the continent.&#x201d;</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To accelerate locally driven humanitarian innovation by developing a local innovation ecosystem so that local communities are strengthen to address their own challenges</narrative>
  </description>
